<h1 class='page_title'>Rules of the Road</h1>
<div class='gradient_line_half'></div>
	<p>
	This page summarizes the rules related to governing SPASE, including
	how changes are voted on and passed for implementation as well as the
	general schedule of these releases.
	</p>
</header>

<section id='page_body'>
<article class='page_body_article'>
<section class='article_body'>
<div class='wysiwyg_content'>

<h2>STEP 1: Proposing a Change to the SPASE Schema</h2>
	<ul>
    	<li class="">Submit a written proposal to <a href="https://groups.io/g/spase">spase@groups.io</a> prior to the monthly SPASE meeting. Your proposal should include:</li>
		<ul>
			<li>Enumeration list additions:</li>
			<ul>
				<li>Name of the enumeration list</li>
				<li>Proposed new term and its definition</li>
			</ul>
			<li>Enumeration list changes:</li>
			<ul>
				<li>Name of the enumeration list</li>
				<li>Old definition</li>
				<li>Proposed new definition</li>
			</ul>
			<li>Schema additions:</li>
			<ul>
				<li>An explanation of the addition and how it will benefit the SPASE schema</li>
				<li>A definition of new terms and the cardinalities -- whether it should be required or optional, and if it should be repeatable.</li>
			</ul>
			<li>Schema changes:</li>
			<ul>
				<li>An explanation of the change and how it will benefit the SPASE schema</li>
				<li>A definition for the changes and, if applicable, the change to the cardinalities</li>
			</ul>
		</ul>
    </ul>
 
<h2>STEP 2: Discussion and Initial Vote</h2>
	<ul>
    	<li class="">The proposal will be discussed at the next available SPASE meeting. Following the SPASE meeting, a voting form will be created and sent to the SPASE Group for voting.</li>
		<li class="">Pollers have the option of "yes", "no", or "maybe".</li>
		<ul>
			<li>Those who vote "maybe" should detail any concerns in a provided text box.</li>
			<li>Those who are ambivalent about their answer should abstain from voting.</li>
		</ul>
    </ul>

<h2>STEP 3: Vote Summary</h2>
	<ul>
    	<li class="">At the next SPASE meeting, the vote will be discussed.</li>
		<li class="">If the vote does not pass unanimously, the concerns will be discussed. The proposal will either remain as is, or there may be modifications.</li>
		<li class="">If all are in agreement, a verbal vote will take place. At this point, the pass threshold will be <em>80%*</em></li>
		<ul>
			<li><em>*80%</em> based on the average of the last 3 SPASE meetings</li>
		</ul>
    </ul>


<h2>STEP 4: Changes are Implemented According to the Minor Schema Change Schedule.</h2>
